cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "Staging Localization & Zero-Model Controls for Connectome-Constrained Controllers"
abstract: >-
  A methodology package for localizing where information is lost in a neural
  pipeline, and for testing structural claims against strong null models.
  Includes five pre-registered negative results from a project that attempted to
  drive a 29-DoF humanoid with a Drosophila whole-brain connectome, and a
  24-source survey annotated by interface paradigm.
authors:
  - name: "fly_brain_boxing contributors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/ljjohn77/connectome-null-controls"
keywords:
  - connectome
  - neural controller
  - null models
  - reproducibility
  - negative results
  - Drosophila
  - spiking neural network
